         the joint probability collapses to near zero on a small sample.
      2. GEX regime was treated as a hard binary gate. When GEX data is missing or
         flat (== 0), the regime never matched either branch -> all signals dropped.
      3. EMA_200 warmup: on a 1-week 1m/3m window there are not enough bars to
         produce a stable EMA_200, so `EMA_50 > EMA_200` was almost never true.
      4. ATR band filter rejected the majority of bars during low-vol sessions.
      5. Macro/event pause flags defaulted to False (trading disabled) when the
         calendar feed was absent.

    Fix strategy (keeps confluence integrity, restores trade flow):
      - Soften hard gates into scored confluence with a minimum score threshold.
      - Treat missing GEX as NEUTRAL (allow both regimes) instead of blocking.
      - Use adaptive EMA fast/slow when EMA_200 is not yet warmed up.
      - Widen ATR band and make it a score contributor, not a hard reject.
      - Default macro/event flags to permissive when data is unavailable.
